      "role": "user",
      "content": "Okay, I hear you on the Tenth Amendment. But look, if the legal basis is a \"legitimate constitutional concern,\" then why does it seem like the framework for this bill is being framed as the \"corrective\" measure while the state-level protections are framed as \"barriers\"? If I'm looking at this objectively, shouldn't we be weighing the validity of the federal government's ability to monitor elections against the states' right to secure them? Which side's logic is actually more consistent with how the Constitution has been interpreted historically?",
